                <pb facs="0514" n="378" xml:id="pg378"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">580.7A3/413: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-15T18:00:00-05:00">April 15, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>84. Your telegram No. 84, April 14, 8 p.m. You may accept the first proposal,
                    that is to agree to the adoption of the clause which reads: “Each country shall
                    be entitled to one vote.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
